    "status": "working-edition",
    "notes": "The prayer said somewhat bowed — aliquantulum inclinatus — at the middle of the altar, gathering the whole offertory into one offering. Its own document: it stands after the Lavábo, between it and the turn to the people. Witness do prints Joannis and Baptistæ without their accents where the same file writes Joánni Baptístæ at the Confíteor; adjudicated in the apparatus. (That witness spells the consonant j throughout, as its own files do; this edition prints i — the apparatus records the difference by declared rule.) ISTÓRUM at w037 is the demonstrative of what is near at hand and refers to the saints whose relics are in the altar — the corpus records the same reference at ordinarium.aufer-a-nobis w029-w032, quorum relíquiæ hic sunt. PROFÍCIAT at w043 with its datives repeats the construction of ordinarium.suscipe-sancte-pater w047, ut mihi et illis profíciat ad salútem. ILLI at w051 is nominative plural, subject of dignéntur, not the dative singular the same form allows; ILLIS at w042 is dative plural. CÆLIS at w057 takes the masculine of the plural, as the corpus records for cælum, neuter in the singular and masculine in the plural. EÚNDEM at w064 is idem, is with the ending -dem, and its m assimilates before d. The demonstrative hic, hæc, hoc carries the plain lemma key hic — SCHEMA.md gives the bare key to the word a reader is likelier to look up — while the adverb lives under hic_adverbium (so at ordinarium.aufer-a-nobis w031). Discriminated keys map back through LEMMA_ALIASES, and the analyzers vote on both.",
